Fixed. All `go test ./server/...` packages now pass.

**Root cause:** In `server/create.go` (`ggufLayersWithMediaType`), the media-type classification for GGUF blobs only treated a file as a projector when `general.type == "projector"` (or it had a standalone `vision.block_count`). Multimodal projector files (mmproj) use `general.type == "mmproj"`, so they were misclassified as `application/vnd.ollama.image.model`, giving them wrong layer accounting.

**Fix** (one line, `server/create.go:1235`):

```go
} else if (f.KV().Uint("block_count") == 0 && f.KV().Uint("vision.block_count") > 0) || f.KV().Kind() == "projector" || f.KV().Kind() == "mmproj" {
```

Now files with `general.type` of either `projector` or `mmproj` are classified as `application/vnd.ollama.image.projector`, which makes `TestGGUFLayersClassifiesMMProjAsProjector` pass along with the rest of the suite.
